# Per-sleeve kill-switch — the repository ceiling for which strategy publishers run.
#
# Flip a sleeve to "off" and redeploy to retire it. Unlike `systemctl disable` by hand
# (which the next deploy silently re-enables), this SURVIVES deploys: the deploy enables
# only the "on" sleeves and `disable --now`s the "off" ones, and the verify + the liveness
# watchdog stop expecting them.
#
# SAFETY — what "off" does and does NOT do:
#   * "off" stops the strategy's target publisher -> NO NEW strategy decisions.
#   * It does NOT publish zero targets, flatten venue exposure, or erase the last accepted
#     component target. Before retirement, explicitly target every owned component to zero
#     and verify the canonical account journal and Bybit are flat.
#   * The single demo account owner remains the only venue mutator and continues account
#     reconciliation plus exchange-native disaster protection. Strategy TP/max-hold logic
#     cannot advance while its publisher is off, so owner protection is not a substitute
#     for the explicit flatten transaction above.
#   * The BTC/ETH hedge publisher rides CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE. Turning CONTINUOUS off also stops
#     hedge retargeting; flatten the hedge target through the account inbox and verify the
#     aggregate account position before retiring CONTINUOUS.
#
# Accepted values: on | off  (also 1/true/yes == on). Per-host overrides live in
# /etc/liquidity-migration/sleeves.env, but they can only NARROW a repo-on sleeve
# to off. A repo-side off is a hard ceiling and a stale host "on" cannot resurrect it.
# Deploy writes the final resolved values to /etc/liquidity-migration/sleeves.resolved.env
# for systemd units to consume.
#
# Strict KEY=value only. Deploy/verify parse this file as data, and the liveness
# watchdog reads the resolved output as a systemd EnvironmentFile. Shell syntax,
# expansion, duplicate keys, and unknown keys are rejected.

# LONG = long-native v11a demo + paper target publishers (a diversifier overlay).
# FORWARD-DEMO STARTED
# 2026-06-04 on this box (first time). "on" shares the one netted demo
# account's margin with CONTINUOUS under the shared account risk policy. Flip to off only
# after publishing zero targets and verifying the owner and venue flat.
# RE-ENABLED 2026-06-16 by operator. The v11a demo publisher uses ENTRY_LEVERAGE=10
# and caps its own projected margin at MAX_PROJECTED_INITIAL_MARGIN_PCT_EQUITY=0.5;
# the account kernel independently enforces account-wide limits. Demo only,
# REAL_MONEY=false. The STATE.md "LONG leverage/capital" decision = this current sizing.
LONG_SLEEVE=on
# CONTINUOUS = continuous-fade DEMO target publisher.
# ON 2026-06-09 by EXPLICIT operator instruction; LONG was re-enabled 2026-06-16.
# This sleeve publishes desired demo components; only the account owner turns accepted
# aggregate targets into Bybit orders. Its paper shadow publishes to the separate shared
# paper owner. Demo account only (REAL_MONEY=false); demo fills are execution evidence,
# not alpha proof. The current
# continuous_ensemble_v2 profile includes the 2026-06-25
# CTRL_BTC_RISK_70_90_35 BTC-risk sizing override. The rmom panel is the
# post-look-ahead-fix shift3 causal build.
CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE=on
# CONTINUOUS_PAPER = target-publishing paper shadow of the demo book (the unit pins
# STRATEGY_PROFILE=continuous_ensemble_v2, mirroring demo). This can run while
# CONTINUOUS_SLEEVE stays off. It publishes to the paper inbox; the deterministic
# paper owner, not the sleeve, owns fills and canonical P&L. It feeds paper/demo
# reconciliation and execution-drift evidence without touching the demo account.
CONTINUOUS_PAPER_SLEEVE=on
